    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d449">

                <pb facs="0627" n="551" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg551"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.00F/219</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by Mr. Joseph G. Green of the Division of
                        Western European Affairs</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-06-06">June 6, 1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Rossi Longhi<anchor n="43" xml:id="d449-f1"/> called me by telephone this
                    afternoon. He told me that the Embassy had just received a telegram from the
                    Foreign Office stating that Ungarelli had been transferred and that his transfer
                    would be effective as soon as the Vice Consul who is to take his place was able
                    to reach his post.</p>
                <p>I told Rossi Longhi that I was pleased to have that information as the long delay
                    had been causing us embarrassment. I asked him when the actual departure of
                    Ungarelli from Detroit could be expected.</p>
                <p>Rossi Longhi replied that he did not know exactly when Ungarelli’s departure
                    would occur; that the man who is to replace him is Vice Consul Enrico
                    Guastone-Belcredi, now stationed in Ottawa, and that he supposed that
                    Guastone-Belcredi would arrive in Detroit in about a month.</p>
                <p>I asked Rossi Longhi whether we could inform our correspondents of Ungarelli’s
                    impending departure. He replied in the affirmative saying that Ungarelli’s
                    transfer had been announced in Rome.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph C. Green</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
